  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n`ProgressiveCurve.previewWithdraw` (lines 148–158) reverts when `totalShares` is at the production floor (`minShare = 1e6`) and `assets` is a small value (e.g., 1 wei). This occurs because `PCMath.square(wrap(totalShares))` rounds down to zero in UD60x18, while `PCMath.divUp(wrap(assets), HALF_SLOPE)` rounds up to at least 1, leading to an underflow in `sub(0, 1)`. The function should return 0 shares in such edge cases, as per the invariant stated in the contest: *\"redeem/convert-to-assets path uses consistent conservative rounding and must not revert in low-share edge cases where result should be zero (PR #136 behavior).\"* The revert violates this invariant, potentially breaking integrations that rely on `previewWithdraw` for estimations or UIs.\n\n**Impact:** The function becomes unusable for valid low-share inputs, affecting availability and correctness of the curve math. While no funds are directly at risk, the protocol's intended behavior is broken.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nModify `previewWithdraw` to handle the case where `square(s) < deduct` gracefully, returning 0 shares:\n\n```solidity\nUD60x18 s = wrap(totalShares);\nUD60x18 deduct = PCMath.divUp(wrap(assets), HALF_SLOPE);\nUD60x18 sq = PCMath.square(s);\nif (unwrap(sq) < unwrap(deduct)) {\n    return 0;\n}\nUD60x18 inner = sub(sq, deduct);\nUD60x18 sharesUD = sub(s, sqrt(inner));\nshares = unwrap(sharesUD);",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { BaseTest } from \"./BaseTest.t.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCCore is BaseTest {\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        // Production minShare = 1e6 (ghost shares floor)\n        // square(wrap(1e6)) rounds to 0 in UD60x18\n        // divUp(wrap(1), HALF_SLOPE) rounds up to 1\n        // sub(0, 1) → arithmetic underflow → revert\n        // Expected: return 0 shares (per PR #136 invariant)\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        progressiveCurve.previewWithdraw(1, 1, 1e6);\n    }\n}",
